I know you've got KERS,

997
00:58:54,699 --> 00:58:56,265
I know you've got
a 6.3-litre V12,

998
00:58:56,266 --> 00:58:58,836
and I know that launch
control system is amazing,

999
00:58:58,871 --> 00:59:00,236
but it's all let down

1000
00:59:00,237 --> 00:59:02,205
by the sponginess
of the Adidas shoe.

1001
00:59:02,206 --> 00:59:04,406
So they should sell you
the car and the shoes.

1002
00:59:04,441 --> 00:59:06,977
No, have you got the correct
shoes and have you worn them in?

1003
00:59:07,012 --> 00:59:09,012
- Exactly.
- Fresh shoes, lads.

1004
00:59:09,013 --> 00:59:13,217
- I just need to- - You need
to skid about. There we go.

1005
00:59:13,252 --> 00:59:15,785
With that sorted,

1006
00:59:15,820 --> 00:59:18,020
it was time to bring in
a racing driver

1007
00:59:18,055 --> 00:59:21,658
to see which of our cars
could do the fastest lap.

1008
00:59:21,693 --> 00:59:24,979
Our resident American
said he wasn't interested,

1009
00:59:25,014 --> 00:59:28,265
because all three cars
are probably communist.

1010
00:59:28,300 --> 00:59:31,636
So instead, we went
for a Belgian chap-

1011
00:59:31,671 --> 00:59:33,169
[GUNFIRE]

1012
00:59:33,170 --> 00:59:36,807
...who's done Formula One
and Formula E,

1013
00:59:36,842 --> 00:59:39,343
Jerome d'Ambrosio.

1014
00:59:44,314 --> 00:59:46,015
Jerome took the cars out

1015
00:59:46,016 --> 00:59:48,686
to get a sense of how
they handled.

1016
01:00:05,002 --> 01:00:06,854
And when he'd finished,

1017
01:00:06,855 --> 01:00:08,765
we were interested to hear

1018
01:00:08,766 --> 01:00:10,641
his professional opinion.

1019
01:00:10,642 --> 01:00:12,943
[SPEAKS FRENCH]

1020
01:00:54,785 --> 01:00:57,938
RICHARD: At this point,
word reached us that Jeremy

1021
01:00:57,973 --> 01:01:01,091
was taking liberties
with the subtitling machine.

1022
01:01:02,459 --> 01:01:05,429
So we moved on
to the big event:

1023
01:01:05,464 --> 01:01:08,098
the timed laps.

1024
01:01:13,437 --> 01:01:15,472
Once the mechanics had
finished their preparations,

1025
01:01:15,507 --> 01:01:18,408
the three speed traps
were activated.

1026
01:01:21,879 --> 01:01:24,548
And the Ferrari LaFerrari
took its place

1027
01:01:24,583 --> 01:01:27,051
on the start line.

1028
01:01:28,185 --> 01:01:30,185
Look how good it looks there.

1029
01:01:30,220 --> 01:01:33,557
This is just wasting time.
It's wasting rubber and fuel.

1030
01:01:33,592 --> 01:01:35,391
No, this is like
an amuse-bouche.

1031
01:01:35,392 --> 01:01:39,096
Yeah, it is. You have ordered
the duck and sherry trifle.

1032
01:01:39,131 --> 01:01:42,833
- And you're a melon ball.
- I'm not even listening.

1033
01:01:45,770 --> 01:01:47,938
[BEEPING]

1034
01:01:58,448 --> 01:02:03,453
Gentlemen, it is doing
231.4 kilometers an hour

1035
01:02:03,488 --> 01:02:05,554
at the end of the straight.

1036
01:02:05,589 --> 01:02:09,193
It's about the same speed as a
Golf diesel, something like that.

1037
01:02:22,840 --> 01:02:26,241
194.9.

1038
01:02:26,276 --> 01:02:28,111
Going down the hill
using gravity.

1039
01:02:28,112 --> 01:02:30,314
- Is he stopping off for shopping?
- He must be.

1040
01:02:45,963 --> 01:02:48,098
Here he is.

1041
01:02:54,604 --> 01:02:59,343
- James, if you want to get a cup of tea.
- We've warmed the track.

1042
01:02:59,378 --> 01:03:02,864
RICHARD: Next it was the turn
of the Porsche 918.

1043
01:03:02,899 --> 01:03:06,350
How much faster will it go
because of the stripes?

1044
01:03:06,385 --> 01:03:08,385
Much.

1045
01:03:22,299 --> 01:03:24,133
231 point...

1046
01:03:24,134 --> 01:03:26,170
So he's faster
than the Ferrari.

1047
01:03:35,679 --> 01:03:38,147
RICHARD: 183.0.

1048
01:03:38,182 --> 01:03:41,750
Way, way,
way slower than him.

1049
01:03:41,785 --> 01:03:43,921
Don't forget between here
and the next measuring point,

1050
01:03:43,956 --> 01:03:46,555
Okay, you've got
four slow corners,

1051
01:03:46,590 --> 01:03:49,259
and those are the ones where the
Porsche is gonna make up time.

1052
01:03:51,161 --> 01:03:52,396
Because of the
four-wheel steering.

1053
01:03:52,397 --> 01:03:56,033
- Like a Honda Prelude?
- No!

1054
01:04:09,646 --> 01:04:12,414
- 110 point what?
- One.

1055
01:04:12,449 --> 01:04:16,386
So, almost to a tenth of a kilometer
an hour, the same speed as you.

1056
01:04:21,258 --> 01:04:24,061
RICHARD: Here he comes.
He's firing noises.

1057
01:04:25,362 --> 01:04:27,362
There it is.
Look at that.

1058
01:04:29,833 --> 01:04:33,337
JEREMY: Finally, it was
the turn of the psycho killer.

1059
01:04:33,372 --> 01:04:36,040
The trickiest,
the edgiest of the three.

1060
01:04:37,541 --> 01:04:39,442
But I was so confident
it'd win,

1061
01:04:39,443 --> 01:04:43,047
I was prepared
to take a massive gamble.

1062
01:04:44,381 --> 01:04:48,168
If the McLaren
isn't the fastest,

1063
01:04:48,203 --> 01:04:51,956
you two can knock
my house down.

1064
01:04:51,991 --> 01:04:54,089
- What?
- Knock it down.

1065
01:04:54,124 --> 01:04:56,959
- What, your house?
- Yeah, and I mean that.

1066
01:04:56,994 --> 01:05:00,664
That's how confident I am
that that will be the fastest.

1067
01:05:00,699 --> 01:05:04,801
- You know we will do that?
- Yeah.

1068
01:05:04,836 --> 01:05:07,236
- It's a serious bet?
- Yeah.

1069
01:05:07,271 --> 01:05:09,840
- Fine.
- If that's not the fastest,

1070
01:05:09,875 --> 01:05:12,259
- we can knock your house down?
- Yup.

1071
01:05:12,294 --> 01:05:14,644
You know where it is.
You've both been.

1072
01:05:14,679 --> 01:05:16,679
I'd love to knock it down.

1073
01:05:23,020 --> 01:05:25,222
Here we go.
A lot riding on this.

1074
01:05:37,834 --> 01:05:41,270
235.9.

1075
01:05:41,305 --> 01:05:44,008
Okay, it's fastest at the end
of the first straight.

1076
01:05:48,712 --> 01:05:50,747
Would you like to come
to my house for dinner?

1077
01:05:50,782 --> 01:05:52,782
Yes. Can I bring a bulldozer?

1078
01:06:00,324 --> 01:06:02,191
188.3.

1079
01:06:02,192 --> 01:06:04,228
That is worryingly quick.
Brisk.

1080
01:06:04,263 --> 01:06:06,062
It's quite brisk?

1081
01:06:06,063 --> 01:06:08,749
We don't know how fast it's
going around the tight turns.

1082
01:06:08,784 --> 01:06:11,435
Might have been doing two
kilometers an hour around here.

1083
01:06:23,180 --> 01:06:24,932
Where is he?

1084
01:06:24,933 --> 01:06:26,933
Crashed.

1085
01:06:44,068 --> 01:06:46,936
With that,
back to the tent.

1086
01:06:46,971 --> 01:06:49,539
[CHEERING]

1087
01:06:54,811 --> 01:06:56,645
Thank you so much. Now...

1088
01:06:56,646 --> 01:06:58,681
I want to make it
absolutely plain,

1089
01:06:58,716 --> 01:07:00,716
'cause I know this matters
to anoraks,

1090
01:07:00,717 --> 01:07:06,156
all three cars were running on
exactly the same sort of tires.

1091
01:07:06,191 --> 01:07:08,758
Yes, same tires, same track,
same driver.

1092
01:07:08,793 --> 01:07:11,060
So the times
are down to the cars.

1093
01:07:11,095 --> 01:07:14,331
Yup. And now it is time
to reveal those times.

1094
01:07:14,366 --> 01:07:16,533
Let me just make it
absolutely clear.

1095
01:07:16,568 --> 01:07:18,101
We don't know what they are.

1096
01:07:18,102 --> 01:07:20,270
The producers have kept them
from us.

1097
01:07:20,305 --> 01:07:22,073
- They're top secret.
- Yup.

1098
01:07:22,074 --> 01:07:23,807
So, let's put
the scoreboard up,

1099
01:07:23,808 --> 01:07:25,007
and let's begin with

1100
01:07:25,008 --> 01:07:27,561
the Ferrari LaFerrari,
I believe.

1101
01:07:27,596 --> 01:07:30,114
Let's see what it did it in,
please.

1102
01:07:33,883 --> 01:07:36,603
We don't know
if that's any good, do we?

1103
01:07:36,638 --> 01:07:39,323
Let's move on
and do the Porsche next.

1104
01:07:39,358 --> 01:07:41,358
What did the Porsche
do it in?

1105
01:07:42,192 --> 01:07:45,862
Oh, yes! 1:54.2!

1106
01:07:45,897 --> 01:07:49,498
Yes! Yes! You see?

1107
01:07:49,533 --> 01:07:51,633
You said it would mince
the Porsche.

1108
01:07:51,668 --> 01:07:55,038
And it didn't mince it.
It was slower than the Porsche.

1109
01:07:55,073 --> 01:07:56,940
I told you
it's just a melon ball.

1110
01:07:56,941 --> 01:07:58,841
It's slower than my car,

1111
01:07:58,842 --> 01:08:01,343
which was faster
than your car.

1112
01:08:01,378 --> 01:08:03,578
0.2 of a second,
and it looks better.

1113
01:08:03,613 --> 01:08:06,350
Yeah, it did in my mirror where
it belongs getting smaller.

1114
01:08:06,385 --> 01:08:07,985
It's a melon ball,
and it lost.

1115
01:08:07,986 --> 01:08:09,185
- Hammond.
- What?

1116
01:08:09,186 --> 01:08:10,705
- Calm down.
- All right.

1117
01:08:10,706 --> 01:08:12,248
Because now we must bring up

1118
01:08:12,249 --> 01:08:14,771
the time that really matters.

1119
01:08:14,806 --> 01:08:16,584
The one where
a lot's at stake.

1120
01:08:16,585 --> 01:08:18,329
The McLaren...
[CLEARS THROAT]

1121
01:08:18,330 --> 01:08:19,462
The McLaren P1.

1122
01:08:19,463 --> 01:08:22,166
- Are you nervous? Sure?
- No. No.

1123
01:08:22,201 --> 01:08:23,499
- A little bit?
- No!

1124
01:08:23,500 --> 01:08:25,019
- I'm not nervous.
- Why be nervous?

1125
01:08:25,020 --> 01:08:26,504
You could get, like,
a shopping trolley

1126
01:08:26,505 --> 01:08:28,670
and keep all your things
in it.

1127
01:08:28,705 --> 01:08:31,540
Make some new friends
under a bridge somewhere.

1128
01:08:31,575 --> 01:08:33,843
- Hammond.
- I'd say sell your body but don't do that.

1129
01:08:33,878 --> 01:08:36,545
Be quiet! Let's-

1130
01:08:36,580 --> 01:08:39,316
Let's bring up the time
of the P1. Here we go.

1131
01:08:39,351 --> 01:08:42,419
- Oh, God.
- Where is it?

1132
01:08:46,823 --> 01:08:49,642
[UPROAR]

1133
01:08:49,677 --> 01:08:52,462
Yes!

1134
01:08:56,666 --> 01:08:59,936
That is funny.
Because you said...

1135
01:08:59,971 --> 01:09:03,207
the fastest,
but it's not the fastest.

1136
01:09:03,242 --> 01:09:05,208
It's the slowest!

1137
01:09:05,209 --> 01:09:08,445
Ladies and gentlemen,
journalist, broadcaster

1138
01:09:08,480 --> 01:09:11,881
and homeless man,
Jeremy Clarkson.

1139
01:09:11,916 --> 01:09:13,916
[CHEERING]

1140
01:09:18,788 --> 01:09:23,525
That's what it is.
That's what it is.

1141
01:09:23,560 --> 01:09:26,363
You're not really going
to knock my house down?

1142
01:09:26,398 --> 01:09:28,830
Yes, we are.

1143
01:09:28,865 --> 01:09:30,865
- A bet is a bet.
- That's the deal.

1144
01:09:30,900 --> 01:09:33,570
- And we're going to film it.
- No, but the thing is,

1145
01:09:33,605 --> 01:09:36,240
on the tires that the
McLaren can be bought with,

1146
01:09:36,275 --> 01:09:38,540
it was faster.

1147
01:09:38,575 --> 01:09:40,977
We agreed right at the start

1148
01:09:41,012 --> 01:09:43,345
we'd all run on
the same tires.

1149
01:09:43,380 --> 01:09:45,849
That was the deal
before your car lost.

1150
01:09:45,884 --> 01:09:47,383
So let's just...

1151
01:09:47,384 --> 01:09:50,887
Let's just sum this
first show up, shall we?

1152
01:09:50,922 --> 01:09:52,721
I've lost my house.

1153
01:09:52,722 --> 01:09:55,091
- We've had a fight with the audience.
- Big one.

1154
01:09:55,126 --> 01:09:57,926
Somebody shot our drone down.

1155
01:09:57,961 --> 01:10:00,664
And we've killed three
quite major celebrities.

1156
01:10:00,699 --> 01:10:02,800
Yeah, but on the plus side,

1157
01:10:02,835 --> 01:10:04,901
my Porsche was the fastest!

1158
01:10:04,936 --> 01:10:06,936
[CHEERING]

1159
01:10:10,407 --> 01:10:12,576
And on that terrible
disappointment,

1160
01:10:12,611 --> 01:10:14,643
I'm afraid it's time to end.

1161
01:10:14,678 --> 01:10:16,514
Thank you all very much
for coming.

1162
01:10:16,515 --> 01:10:18,013
Thank you for watching.

1163
01:10:18,014 --> 01:10:19,917
And we'll see you next week
in Johannesburg.

1164
01:10:19,918 --> 01:10:21,469
Good-bye!

1165
01:10:21,470 --> 01:10:23,470
[CHEERING]

